    "title": "Data from the article \"DTL-IceNet: A Dual-Task Learning Architecture with Multi-Scale Fusion Mechanisms for Enhanced Ice Detection on Transmission Lines\"",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15718305",
    "publication_date": "2025-06-23",
    "description": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h2>Description of the data and file structure</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>example_icing_images: This dataset contains images of transmission line icing of various types, used for ice layer recognition and thickness detection tasks.</li>\n<li>Ice_code: The above code is a semantic segmentation model based on the ground truth image of the power grid ice-covered line. By combining the deep learning model with the multimodal branch, the refined segmentation of the ice-covered contour is achieved. The nes folder contains the entire model structure and detailed codes of each module. For other usage methods, please refer to the README.</li>\n</ol>",
